cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, cite this project and the original datasets and backbones."
title: "POLAR Posture Recognition: Audited DINOv2 and ConvNeXt Benchmarks"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Huseyinli
    given-names: Abdulla
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/polar-posture-recognition"
url: "https://github.com/abdullahuseyinli-dot/polar-posture-recognition"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Source-overlap-audited four-class POLAR posture classification with adapted
  DINOv2 and ConvNeXt, frozen multilayer feature classifiers and a locked ensemble.
  The ensemble achieves 93.988333 percent macro-F1 on 3,329 held-out images.
  Includes a separately evaluated person-level V-COCO transfer study and later
  matched DINOv2, DINOv3 and SigLIP2 development comparisons. Version 1.0.0
  identifies this standalone project, preserving the original study versions.
  The custom tasks do not establish a standard POLAR or V-COCO leaderboard rank.
keywords:
  - posture recognition
  - POLAR
  - DINOv2
  - DINOv3
  - ConvNeXt
  - SigLIP2
  - V-COCO
  - calibrated ensembles
  - source-overlap audit
  - reproducible evaluation
